(:id "port/python/vt/variable-class" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/vtpointerarrays_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtPointerArraysRows/variable-class (graph_tree, graph_shared, graph_empty, graph_deep, guard_false_no_edge, guard_true_both_edges, list_shared, list_before_pointer, and the blobs_pointers construct)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/vtpointerarrays_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtPointerArraysRowsNegativeControl/shared-node-renumbered/variable-class, /pointer-array-index-shifted/variable-class" "make python-vt-pointer-arrays-rows python-vt-pointer-arrays-rows-negative-control (make/python-vt-pointer-arrays-rows.mk)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/pointerarrays_test.go: TestPythonVtPointerArrays, TestPythonVtPointerArraysNegativeControl") :tested-revision "ef2a7ceb0f4fbed0755e0998220880df484ce3a9" :note "2026-11-17: every variable-class manifest row luatable's vtcells_test.go names, and the Go-engine construct blobs_pointers, read through the generated Root.load and saved back byte-identical to the Go engine's canonical wire, measure equal to length, a second save equal to the first, and the engine's widened and unknown counters, on the flat node table with shared nodes kept as one record; no row refuses. The negative control numbers a shared node again at each reach in a copy of the save (graph_shared and list_shared go red by name) and writes a pointer array's indices one past their node (blobs_pointers goes red). Run on macOS arm64 under both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2, make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
(:id "port/python/vt/pointer-arrays" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/vtpointerarrays_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtPointerArraysRows/pointer-arrays (stream_parts, stream_chain, parts_elem_kind, parts_count_past_bound, parts_index_out_of_range, w1_fleet, w2_fleet, and every other manifest row whose root reaches a pointer array, with a completeness check over the manifest; and the blobs_pointers construct)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/vtpointerarrays_rows_test.go: TestPythonVtPointerArraysRowsNegativeControl/pointer-array-bound-off/pointer-arrays, /index-past-node-table-off/pointer-arrays, /pointer-array-index-shifted/pointer-arrays" "make python-vt-pointer-arrays-rows python-vt-pointer-arrays-rows-negative-control (make/python-vt-pointer-arrays-rows.mk)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/pointerarrays_test.go: TestPythonVtPointerArrays, TestPythonVtPointerArraysNegativeControl") :tested-revision "ef2a7ceb0f4fbed0755e0998220880df484ce3a9" :note "2026-11-17: 22 manifest rows (every row whose root reaches a []*T, [N]*T, [..N]*T or [Min..N]*T, the cross-version fleet and streamdemo arm rows among them) and the blobs_pointers construct are each held to the Go engine's verdict on the same wire: accepted rows save byte-identical to its canonical wire with its counters, and parts_elem_kind, parts_count_past_bound and parts_index_out_of_range refuse as reports.txt says with the caller's buffer and LoadReport untouched. The negative control drops the bounded count check (parts_count_past_bound red), drops the graph judge's index-past-the-node-table check (parts_index_out_of_range red) and shifts each written element index by one (stream_parts and blobs_pointers red), each in a copy of the runtime. Run on macOS arm64 under both pinned interpreters (CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2, make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
